# Line endings
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on the Windows workstation. Without the rules below, a
# checkout there rewrites LF to CRLF, and two files break as a result:
#
#   - `pre-push` gets a CRLF after `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, and git refuses the
#     hook with "bad interpreter". This is the fix referred to in
#     `workstation/claude/setup/windows.md`.
#   - Python scripts show every line as modified when the same file is edited
#     on another machine, which buries real diffs.
#
# Scoped deliberately to the files that break. A blanket `* text=auto eol=lf`
# would also rewrite the markdown corpus, which nothing here needs.

pre-push  text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
